diff --git a/docs/business-rules.md b/docs/business-rules.md
index 7a3126a..ac3b7d5 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -72,9 +72,22 @@ ### Ticket
 Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
+- Display code — per-queue sequence (see below).
 - Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Issuance timestamp `issued_at` (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` (default) or `printed`.
+- Status: `waiting` (on issuance) or `called`. There is no cancelled status.
+- Call fields `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`, filled when called.
+
+**Queue:** belongs to one entity; has a `name`, a `slug` unique within the entity, an `is_active` flag (default true) and optional `labels_i18n` (JSON).
+
+**Display code:** `A001`, `A002`, … per queue (prefix `A`, at least 3 digits, zero padded; beyond 999 it grows: `A1000`). Unique per `(queue_id, code)`. The next code is "last valid code + 1" by **insertion order** (not string order: `A999` then `A1000` yields `A1001`). Deleting a ticket does not reuse its number (`A001..A003` with `A002` deleted → next is `A004`). Codes not matching `A<digits>` are skipped (only `A-X` → next `A001`; `A001` then `A-X` → next `A002`). Implemented by `Ticket::nextCode()`.
+
+**Issuance** (`App\Actions\IssueTicket`): rejects an inactive queue with `InactiveQueueException`; the state is read from the database inside the transaction under a row lock on the queue, never from the caller's possibly stale model, and nothing is persisted on rejection. A unique `(queue_id, code)` collision (concurrent issuance) is retried a few times. A negative priority throws `InvalidArgumentException`. New tickets are `waiting` with `issued_at = now()`, default channel `virtual` and priority `0`.
+
+**Write-once:** after issuance only `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` (and `updated_at`) may change; any Eloquent save/update changing another field throws `LogicException`.
+
+**Single call:** `Ticket::call(User)` marks the ticket `called` and records `called_at` and the caller. Only members of the ticket's entity may call (`AuthorizationException`, ticket unchanged). Calling a ticket that is not `waiting` throws `LogicException` (status re-read under lock, so a stale instance cannot call twice). *Which* ticket to call next (priority/fairness) is not implemented yet.
 
 ### Priority
 
diff --git a/docs/database-schema.md b/docs/database-schema.md
index 770fd91..a801b06 100644
--- a/docs/database-schema.md
+++ b/docs/database-schema.md
@@ -147,9 +147,10 @@ ## Modeling Notes
 - **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). In MVP, "one user per entity" rule is enforced in application; no global UK on `user_id`.
 - **Owner invariant:** `entities` has no `owner_membership_id` FK. The single-owner constraint lives on `entity_memberships` via `entities.owner_seq` (generated `CASE WHEN role='owner' THEN 1 ELSE NULL END`) and a unique `(entity_id, owner_seq)` index — portable across SQLite + MySQL. Bootstrapping creates the entity then its owner row in one transaction; ownership transfer demotes the old owner to `admin` and promotes the target `admin` to `owner` in the same transaction. The generated column goes NULL during both steps, so the transient no-owner state is allowed (only a 2nd `role='owner'` row for the same entity collides).
 - **Numeric priority:** `tickets.priority` is an integer — **higher value, more prioritized**. Named levels (normal/priority/80+) are configurable presets per entity mapping to values; sorting uses the number.
-- **Ticket write-once:** ticket is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. All fields are immutable after issuance, **except** `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`, filled at call time. No call history table.
+- **Ticket write-once:** ticket is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. All fields are immutable after issuance, **except** `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`, filled at call time (enforced by the `Ticket` model: any other change throws `LogicException`). No call history table.
 - **Ticket ↔ totem:** ticket knows only its **queue** (`queue_id`). `channel` records origin type; no FK to `totems`.
-- **Ticket `code`:** displayable password (e.g., `A012`) shown on totem/TV; scope and format per queue/entity.
+- **Ticket `code`:** displayable password shown on totem/TV; per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, … (3+ digits, grows past `A999`), allocated by `Ticket::nextCode()` and unique per `(queue_id, code)`. Collisions from concurrent issuance are retried by `IssueTicket`.
+- **Queues and tickets (implemented):** `queues` (`entity_id` FK cascade, `name`, `slug`, `is_active` default true, `labels_i18n` JSON null, timestamps; unique `(entity_id, slug)`). `tickets` (`queue_id` FK cascade, `code`, `priority` unsigned int default 0, `channel` default `virtual`, `status` default `waiting`, `issued_at`, `called_at` null, `called_by_user_id` FK users null-on-delete, timestamps; unique `(queue_id, code)`, index `(queue_id, status, priority, issued_at)`). `queue_access` and `totems` are not created yet.
 - **Fairness:** 3-ticket priority fairness rule calculated in domain (queue state), no extra table.
 - **Separated finance:** `billing_accounts` (1:0..1 with entity) + `subscriptions` + `plans` isolate financial model. Entity without billing can be created and tested without payment configuration. `payment_options` defines cycle (MONTHLY/ANNUAL), method (PIX/CARD/BOLETO), discount and refund window. `payments` tracks individual charges with `due_date`, `paid_at`, `refund_deadline`. Asaas webhooks update `status` idempotently. `asaas_customer_id` in `billing_accounts`; `asaas_subscription_id` in `subscriptions`; `asaas_payment_id` in `payments`.
 - **Active subscription unique:** `billing_account_id` is UK in `subscriptions` (1:1); payment history in `payments`.
diff --git a/tests/Feature/Ticket/IssueTicketTest.php b/tests/Feature/Ticket/IssueTicketTest.php
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ff6cab4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/Feature/Ticket/IssueTicketTest.php
@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@
+<?php
+
+use App\Actions\IssueTicket;
+use App\Enums\TicketChannel;
+use App\Enums\TicketStatus;
+use App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException;
+use App\Models\Queue;
+use App\Models\Ticket;
+use Illuminate\Database\UniqueConstraintViolationException;
+use Illuminate\Foundation\Testing\RefreshDatabase;
+use Illuminate\Support\Carbon;
+
+uses(RefreshDatabase::class);
+
+test('issues a waiting virtual ticket with defaults', function () {
+    Carbon::setTestNow('2026-10-29 10:00:00');
+    $queue = Queue::factory()->create();
+
+    $ticket = (new IssueTicket)($queue);
+
+    expect($ticket->exists)->toBeTrue()
+        ->and($ticket->queue_id)->toBe($queue->id)
+        ->and($ticket->code)->toBe('A001')
+        ->and($ticket->status)->toBe(TicketStatus::Waiting)
+        ->and($ticket->channel)->toBe(TicketChannel::Virtual)
+        ->and($ticket->priority)->toBe(0)
+        ->and($ticket->issued_at->equalTo(now()))->toBeTrue()
+        ->and($ticket->called_at)->toBeNull()
+        ->and($ticket->called_by_user_id)->toBeNull();
+
+    Carbon::setTestNow();
+});
+
+test('issues sequential codes with the given priority and channel', function () {
+    $queue = Queue::factory()->create();
+    $issue = new IssueTicket;
+
+    $first = $issue($queue, 10, TicketChannel::Totem);
+    $second = $issue($queue, channel: TicketChannel::Printed);
+
+    expect($first->code)->toBe('A001')
+        ->and($first->priority)->toBe(10)
+        ->and($first->channel)->toBe(TicketChannel::Totem)
+        ->and($second->code)->toBe('A002')
+        ->and($second->channel)->toBe(TicketChannel::Printed);
+});
+
+test('rejects an inactive queue and persists nothing', function () {
+    $queue = Queue::factory()->create(['is_active' => false]);
+
+    expect(fn () => (new IssueTicket)($queue))->toThrow(InactiveQueueException::class);
+    expect(Ticket::count())->toBe(0);
+});
+
+test('InactiveQueueException is a RuntimeException', function () {
+    expect(new InactiveQueueException)->toBeInstanceOf(RuntimeException::class);
+});
+
+test('rejects a queue deactivated after the caller loaded it', function () {
+    $queue = Queue::factory()->create();
+    Queue::whereKey($queue->id)->update(['is_active' => false]);
+
+    expect($queue->is_active)->toBeTrue();
+    expect(fn () => (new IssueTicket)($queue))->toThrow(InactiveQueueException::class);
+    expect(Ticket::count())->toBe(0);
+});
+
+test('accepts a queue reactivated after the caller loaded it', function () {
+    $queue = Queue::factory()->create(['is_active' => false]);
+    Queue::whereKey($queue->id)->update(['is_active' => true]);
+
+    expect((new IssueTicket)($queue)->code)->toBe('A001');
+});
+
+test('rejects a negative priority with InvalidArgumentException and persists nothing', function () {
+    $queue = Queue::factory()->create();
+
+    expect(fn () => (new IssueTicket)($queue, -1))->toThrow(InvalidArgumentException::class);
+    expect(Ticket::count())->toBe(0);
+});
+
+test('retries on a code collision from concurrent issuance', function () {
+    $queue = Queue::factory()->create();
+    Ticket::factory()->forQueue($queue)->create();
+    $collide = true;
+
+    // Simulate a concurrent writer having taken the code we computed: the first insert reuses A001.
+    Ticket::creating(function (Ticket $ticket) use (&$collide) {
+        if ($collide) {
+            $collide = false;
+            $ticket->code = 'A001';
+        }
+    });
+
+    $ticket = (new IssueTicket)($queue);
+
+    expect($ticket->code)->toBe('A002')
+        ->and(Ticket::count())->toBe(2);
+});
+
+test('gives up after a few collisions', function () {
+    $queue = Queue::factory()->create();
+    Ticket::factory()->forQueue($queue)->create();
+
+    Ticket::creating(fn (Ticket $ticket) => $ticket->code = 'A001');
+
+    expect(fn () => (new IssueTicket)($queue))->toThrow(UniqueConstraintViolationException::class);
+    expect(Ticket::count())->toBe(1);
+});
